.TH ASYS-FLOW-VIEW 1 "October 2026" "asys" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asys-flow-view \- view and edit asys workflow files, and follow runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asys-flow-view
[\fI\-toolkitoption\fR ...]
[\fB\-environment\fR \fIdir\fR]
.I file.yaml
.br
.B asys-flow-view
[\fI\-toolkitoption\fR ...]
.B \-run
.I run
[\fB\-root\fR \fIdir\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I asys-flow-view
shows an asys workflow file (\fBasys: workflow/1\fR) as a map: steps are
triangles on a rail that runs left to right and wraps into lines, top to
bottom, when it is longer than the window. Hue names the kind of work: green
agents, blue programs, red humans, yellow gateways where the rail forks and
joins. Groups and repeats are flat fields the rail crosses.
.PP
Selecting a step shows its fields in the panel beneath the map, where they can
be edited; problems found by validation are marked on the map and listed in
the panel. Every edit goes to the file's YAML, keeping its comments and order,
and can be undone. Nothing is written until the file is saved.
.PP
With
.BR \-run ,
the program follows a run instead: steps not yet reached are open, finished
ones filled, running ones carry a cursor beneath them, and a failure says so.
Selecting a step shows its jobs, results and the end of their logs. A run is
read only.
.PP
The program is a client of
.BR "asys workflow serve" ,
which it runs as a child and speaks to in lines of JSON on its standard input
and output; that process loads, lays out, edits, validates and saves.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-environment " dir"
Check worker types, program arguments and human forms against the worker
environment in
.IR dir ,
and colour each step by the kind of worker its type is. The default is
.BR $ASYS_ENVIRONMENT_DIR ;
without either, steps are grey and everything but worker types is checked.
.TP
.BI \-run " run"
Follow a run: a run ID, an unambiguous prefix of one, or its directory.
.TP
.BI \-root " dir"
The state directory holding runs, as for
.BR "asys --help" .
.TP
.BI \-service " command"
The model to run, split at spaces; the \fBservice\fR resource.
.TP
.B \-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.PP
The program also accepts the standard X Toolkit options, among them
.BR \-display ,
.BR \-geometry ,
.BR \-iconic ,
.BR \-name ,
.B \-xrm
and
.BR \-fn ;
see
.BR X (7).
.SH "KEYS AND MOUSE"
.TP 12
.B /
Go to a step or command by name; matching letters are enough.
.TP
.B Arrows
Move the selection along the flow: next, previous, above, below.
.TP
.B Return
Edit the selected step's fields; Return commits a field, Tab moves to the
next, Escape returns to the map.
.TP
.B a r c e
Add a step after the selection, rename it, set where it continues, set
where it continues on error.
.TP
.B "Delete, x"
Remove the selected step.
.TP
.B "u, Ctrl-Z"
Undo; \fBCtrl-Y\fR redoes.
.TP
.B Ctrl-S
Save.
.TP
.B "+ \- 0 1"
Zoom in, zoom out, fit the workflow to the window, full size.
.TP
.B Tab
Show or hide the panel.
.TP
.B y
Show or hide the YAML.
.TP
.B q
Quit; with unsaved changes, press it twice.
.PP
Drag from one step to another to connect them; with Shift held, the
connection is the error path. Drag on empty paper, or use the wheel, to
scroll; Ctrl and the wheel zoom. Double-click a call step to open the file it
calls.
.SH RESOURCES
The class is
.BR AsysFlowView .
Every resource the program uses is in its application defaults file, which
documents them; the program carries a copy compiled in. The program's own:
.TP
.B service \fR(class \fBService\fR)
The model command, default
.BR "asys workflow serve" .
.TP
.B environmentDirectory\fR, \fBrun\fR, \fBroot
Set by the options of the same meaning.
.TP
.B titleFont\fR, \fBstepFont
The panel's heading fonts for the workflow and for a step.
.TP
.B map.paper\fR, \fBmap.ink\fR, \fBmap.verde\fR, \fBmap.blu\fR, \fBmap.rosso\fR, \fBmap.giallo
The map's colours; the rails and fields are drawn from paper and ink.
.TP
.B map.sansFont\fR, \fBmap.sansBoldFont\fR, \fBmap.monoFont
The map's typefaces, as fontconfig names.
.PP
For example, in
.IR ~/.Xdefaults :
.PP
.nf
.RS
AsysFlowView.geometry:   1600x1000
AsysFlowView*map.verde:  #2E6B4A
.RE
.fi
.PP
The program answers
.BR editres (1),
which shows its widget tree and changes resources while it runs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X server to use.
.TP
.B XENVIRONMENT
A resource file read in place of the host's defaults; see
.BR X (7).
.TP
.B ASYS_ENVIRONMENT_DIR
The worker environment, when
.B \-environment
is not given: the variable asys sets for its jobs.
.TP
.B ASYS_FLOW_SERVICE
When set, overrides the \fBservice\fR resource.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PREFIX/share/X11/app-defaults/AsysFlowView
The application defaults, found through
.BR XFILESEARCHPATH .
.TP
.I ~/.Xdefaults
Personal resources, loaded with
.BR xrdb (1).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR editres (1),
.BR xrdb (1),
.BR X (7);
.B "asys workflow \-\-help"
for checking and converting workflow files.
.SH BUGS
Labels outside the map use the core X fonts, which are Latin-1.
